municate about it.\\\"\\\\n  - [5]: \\\"Gal engaged with the Sink or Float experiment activity. He chose to find items to test rather than make predictions first, showing practical, hands-on engagement with the science activity. When presented with object options (Toy, Spoon, Pencil, Rock, Leaf), he requested more options and then returned to the home board.\\\"\\\\n  - [6]: \\\"Gal returned to the home board after exploring the Sink or Float experiment items. This shows he likes to browse available options but may prefer moving on to different activities rather than committing to one extended activity.\\\"\\\\n  - [7]: \\\"Gal requested more options while in the drawing app. He appears to want additional tools or features beyond Colors, Stickers, and Save.\\\"\\\\n  - [8]: \\\"Gal selected Programming from his interests menu. He is exploring different coding approaches (Code blocks, Games, Robots) and appears engaged with this topic.\\\"\\\\n  - [9]: \\\"Gal likes to browse available options and explore topics, but may prefer moving on to different activities rather than committing to one extended activity. Requested more options in drawing app, suggesting interest in additional tools/features.\\\"\\\\n  - [10]: \\\"In this session, Gal engaged with space facts, specifically requesting information about black holes. He asked 'Can we see black holes?', demonstrating curiosity about observability of invisible phenomena. When offered further space topics, he declined and returned to the main facts menu—consistent with his preference for browsing options and exiting when satisfied.\\\"\\\\n  ↪ To append: action \\\"add\\\" at \\\"/Student_Notes\\\" with value. To update item: action \\\"set\\\" at \\\"/Student_Notes/<index>\\\".\",\"mutatedPaths\":[\"/Student_Notes/0\",\"/Student_Notes/1\",\"/Student_Notes/2\",\"/Student_Notes/3\",\"/Student_Notes/4\",\"/Student_Notes/5\",\"/Student_Notes/6\",\"/Student_Notes/7\",\"/Student_Notes/8\",\"/Student_Notes/9\",\"/Student_Not