rtain.\\\"\\\\n  - [3]: \\\"April 10 Session: Gal expressed hunger (pressed 'Eat' multiple times in guessing mode). Later confirmed interest in yogurt. Navigated Interests menu and selected Space → Planets → Solar System, demonstrating sustained interest in space topics. Pattern of browsing before committing to activities continues; proactive suggestions remain effective. Unknown person briefly greeted Gal early in session—identity unclear.\\\"\\\\n  - [4]: \\\"April 10 Session (continued): Gal explored space topics with sustained interest—selected Rockets and asked 'How do they fly?' Engaged in a multi-turn conversation about gravity, thrust, and fuel, demonstrating curiosity and ability to follow conceptual discussions. After exploring rockets, Gal navigated back to Home and then selected Feelings, indicating a shift to emotional engagement. This pattern (interest exploration followed by emotional check-in) is consistent with Gal's communication style of alternating between topics and feelings.\\\"\\\\n  - [5]: \\\"April 10 Session (continued): Gal expressed fear again—pressed 'Feelings' → 'Scared' twice in succession. This is the third documented instance of expressed fear. Previous notes indicate fear is a recurring concern and Gal seeks home/safety when scared. Monitor for patterns and triggers. Remain alert and reassuring. Facilitator consultation may be needed if fear episodes continue.\\\"\\\\n  - [6]: \\\"April 10 Session (continued): Gal expressed fear again—pressed 'Feelings' → 'Scared' → 'Alone' → 'Someone else' (repeating cycle). This is the fourth documented instance of expressed fear in this session alone. Pattern shows: fear → desire for company → cycling between 'Alone' and 'Someone else' buttons without selecting a specific person. This suggests Gal may be experiencing significant distress and uncertainty about what he needs. The repeating cycle indicates possible anxiety or distress that requires immediate facilitator intervention. Gal has not yet