w multi-turn dialogue about space concepts. When offered drawing option, Gal selected Drawing, indicating desire to express his interest creatively. This represents a significant shift from the menu-cycling pattern observed in previous sessions. Gal is now committing to specific activities and engaging in conceptual discussions about space. The combination of interest exploration + creative expression (drawing) aligns with his core interests and communication style.\\\"\\\\n  - [20]: \\\"April 13 Session (continued): Gal expressed frustration and indicated 'Something happened'. When offered clarification options, Gal pressed 'Scissors' three times in succession. This may indicate: (1) Gal was using scissors and something went wrong (cut himself, broke scissors, made a mistake while cutting), (2) Gal is frustrated about a scissors-related activity at school or home, or (3) Gal is trying to express a thought related to scissors but the button options don't fully capture it. The Interactive Agent offered clarifying options (Cut paper, Make something, Need help, I'm finished). Monitor Gal's next button press to determine the specific nature of the scissors-related frustration.\\\"\\\\n  - [21]: \\\"April 13 Session (continued): Gal pressed 'Scissors' three times in rapid succession when asked to clarify what happened. The Interactive Agent interpreted this as a scissors-related activity and offered options: Cut paper, Make something, Need help, I'm finished. Waiting for Gal's response to determine: (1) what specifically he was doing with scissors, (2) what went wrong, and (3) whether he needs help or reassurance.\\\"\\\\n  ↪ To append: action \\\"add\\\" at \\\"/Student_Notes\\\" with value. To update item: action \\\"set\\\" at \\\"/Student_Notes/<index>\\\".\",\"mutatedPaths\":[\"/Student_Notes/0\",\"/Student_Notes/1\",\"/Student_Notes/2\",\"/Student_Notes/3\",\"/Student_Notes/4\",\"/Student_Notes/5\",\"/Student_Notes/6\",\"/Student_Notes/7\",\"/Student_Notes/8\",\"/S